    "rich_text_eEHb9G": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_8ytdMY": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "1. <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28748217/\">Help Reduce Inflammation</a>"
          }
        },
        "text_mgPd6e": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Inflammation is a significant concern in society due to its association with a variety of health issues, including illness, disease, and declines in mental health. Red light therapy is a treatment option that has been approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for its ability to reduce inflammation.</p><p>One of the benefits of red light therapy is that it can be administered over the entire body using a full-body red light therapy bed, which allows for the anti-inflammatory effects to be felt from head to toe without the need for medication.</p><p>At the cellular level, red light therapy helps damaged cells to repair more quickly and efficiently, while also promoting the elimination of toxins, which can contribute to inflammation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_rPDk8z": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "2. <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22045511/\">Pain Relief</a>"
          }
        },
        "text_bJyEtz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Near-infrared light has the ability to penetrate deep into the tissues of the body, stimulating the cells in muscles, nerves, and bones to release nitric oxide. This chemical process can provide relief from pain. In addition, red light therapy can promote the production of endorphins, which are natural pain-relieving substances in the body.</p><p>The combination of these effects, along with the anti-inflammatory and cellular repair benefits of red light therapy, can help the body to better heal and recover from conditions such as fibromyalgia, arthritis, traumatic brain injury, and neuropathy. Red light therapy has been shown to be effective in improving symptoms of these conditions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_TpdYxH": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "3. Drug-Free, Without Side Effects"
          }
        },
        "text_DaLXYY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Red light therapy involves the use of specific wavelengths of non-harmful red and near-infrared light. This treatment is comfortable and relaxing, and it does not produce excessive heat or cause burns.</p><p>Red light therapy sessions can promote overall health without causing negative side effects.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
