    "rich_text_FPWJ8f": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_KfG9cx": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "5.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34947870/\"> Boost Your Workouts</a>"
          }
        },
        "text_WXJML9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Red light therapy has been shown to improve endurance and athletic performance, allowing athletes to train harder and longer. Many Olympic and top-level athletes use red light therapy to enhance their training, and some have even gone to great lengths to ensure that they have access to this treatment during competitions.</p><p>For example, a certain U.S. Olympic team had a red light therapy bed shipped to the Rio Olympics in 2016, and the Secretary of State had to become involved to ensure that the cargo was released from customs in time for the athletes to use it.</p><p>In addition to improving athletic performance during training, red light therapy can also facilitate post-exercise recovery, helping athletes to recover more quickly and efficiently after intense workouts.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_KfG9cx",
        "text_WXJML9"
      ],
