    "rich_text_Rqd9BR": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_nXqVcK": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "7. <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33471046/\">Skin Repair & Anti-Aging Effects</a>"
          }
        },
        "text_H8wPGD": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Red light therapy offers a wide range of benefits for the skin. Many estheticians, who are among the early adopters of red light technology, now offer red light therapy treatments as part of their services. They recognize that adding red light therapy to skincare routines can enhance the results of these treatments.</p><p>Red light therapy can help to plump and repair the skin without the need for injections or medication. The red light spectrum penetrates about half an inch into the skin, increasing circulation and reducing inflammation, which can trigger healing at the cellular level.</p><p>Some of the other skin benefits associated with red light therapy include boosting collagen production, reversing sun damage, soothing eczema and acne, reducing the appearance of fine lines, fading scars, and even skin tone. Red light therapy can also be used to promote wound healing and soothe burns.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_nXqVcK",
