    "rich_text_DcCfMy": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_U3VkMm": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "8. <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34420956/\">Improve Circulation</a>"
          }
        },
        "text_AVrm4d": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Red light therapy has been approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for its ability to increase circulation in the body. Scientific research has demonstrated that red light therapy can increase the size of blood vessels and stimulate the growth of new, small blood vessels called capillaries.</p><p>The combination of increased circulation and enhanced cellular oxygen absorption provided by red light therapy can help to speed up wound healing and reduce inflammation. Areas of the body that are prone to poor circulation, such as the lower legs and feet, can particularly benefit from red light therapy treatments.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
